Two directories began as another project
----------------------------------------

`node/` and `helm/charts/flow/contrib-helm-chart/` are forks. Both are
maintained here rather than tracked against the project they came from, both
carry changes made here, and both are covered by the license above like the
rest of the tree.

Each keeps the license file it was obtained under, in place, unchanged. Those
files are not a second set of terms for this tree's version of the code. They
are the notice the original code came with, which the original terms require to
be retained and which those same terms permit this repository to redistribute
under the AGPL. The code as its own copyright holders publish it stays
available from them, on the terms they publish it under.

**`node/` began as Redash** (https://github.com/getredash/redash).
`node/LICENSE` is the two-clause BSD license, copyright (c) 2013-2020 Arik
Fraimovich, all rights reserved, exactly as written there. A redistribution in
source or binary form has to retain that copyright notice, the list of
conditions and the disclaimer. Attribution for what this fork inherited belongs
to the Redash project and its contributors.

**`helm/charts/flow/contrib-helm-chart/` began as the Redash community Helm
chart** (https://github.com/getredash/contrib-helm-chart).
`helm/charts/flow/contrib-helm-chart/LICENSE` is the Apache License, Version
2.0. Apache-2.0 asks that changed files be marked as changed, so: **the files
in that directory have been changed here.** It no longer declares the redis and
postgresql subchart dependencies, and Chart.yaml records why; it carries
templates the chart it was forked from does not have, among them a 1Password
item and a configmap; and its values and its deployment templates have diverged
from that chart. It ships no NOTICE file of its own, so there is no NOTICE text
to propagate.

Both of those license files are the authority on their own wording. The
paragraphs above summarise them and do not replace them.


